OpenBFME Uber performance patch (2026-10-17)
============================================

Base: upstream Open-BFME/openbfme-godot 9451fc8 with the map workshop's four
engine patches (this fork's commits up to 31a4a2a). Apply from the
repository root:  git apply patches/openbfme-uber-performance.patch

What it does. Faithful results are unchanged unless marked "Uber"; Uber stays
deterministic across thread counts and machines (docs/UBER.md):

Pathfinding (lanes PATHPERF-2, PATHPERF-4)
  - the search asks a unit's speed once per search, remembers line-of-sight
    cells while smoothing a path, and keeps the open list's costs beside the
    cells (same paths, about 1.8x faster)
  - the cell-info pool grows past 60,000 records instead of failing
  - Uber: the path queue holds 16,384 requests; a mass order (120+ waiting)
    gets 4x the cell budget until the queue is down to 40
Spatial scans (lane UBER-2A)
  - the nearest-object search skips the exact distance test when a cheap
    bound already rules a unit out; the search heap is reused
  - Uber: scans skip friendly partition layers; the target grid is built
    once per frame
Per-unit work (lane UBER-2B)
  - a geometry keeps its bounding radii; an object keeps its collide
    modules; the physics lookup is reused; the member pass computes its
    angle's cos / sin once
  - Uber: collision pairs whose handlers would all return at once are
    skipped; a melee tick builds its reach candidates once per horde
Recording, hashing and collisions (lane UBER-2C)
  - Uber: a recorded game keeps the state hash of every 5th frame (replays
    compare every recorded hash; saves record their frame's hash)
  - the collision pass tests overlap before sorting the candidates
  - the state hash walks only the AI states that keep fields
Battle pathfinding (lane UBER-3P, Uber only)
  - a search that cannot reach its goal ends once its answer has held for
    256 cells; an attack search without an endpoint likewise
Clash work (lane UBER-3W)
  - an object keeps its attribute modifier module; the collision search
    visits only the buckets a unit's reach touches
  - Uber: collision facts gathered on the job pool, shroud template vision
    kept per record, cheaper large group bonus and amoeba reach scans

Measured (uber bench, map mp fall back 8p, 30 frames, logic wall time per
frame, all logic threads, owner's PC, back to back on a quiet machine):
                       native     patched
  Uber, 10,000 troops  172 ms      70 ms   (2.5x)
  Uber, 30,000 troops  424 ms     129 ms   (3.3x; 1 of 30 frames over 200 ms,
                                            native 30 of 30)
  Faithful, 10,000     135 ms      95 ms   (1.4x)
  Faithful, 30,000     374 ms     243 ms   (1.5x)

Tests: uber1 (pins regenerated for the intended Uber changes; same hashes on
1, 4 and 16 threads), pathperf1, pathfind, perf1, perf2, partition, emotion,
target, horde*, phys1, save2, replay, mp1, net core / net retail (LAN games
between peer processes, desync checks) pass. The online3 / netlag1 relay
tests fail identically on native 9451fc8 on this PC (environment). A
parallel Faithful hash was tried and reverted: it desynced a LAN game.

